      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T23:05:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is blocking the submission of aosp/1465866 and its children. https://android-build.googleplex.com/builds/forrest/run/L79300000720290739 shows the error that I get.\n\nerror: prebuilts/runtime/mainline/runtime/sdk/Android.bp:974:1: module \"runtime-module-sdk_libm@current\" variant \"linux_bionic_arm64_static\": module \"runtime-module-sdk_libc@current\" is not a shared library\n\nIn the build, the linux_bionic_arm64 host target is enabled and therefore `linux_bionic.enabled: true` in the bp file makes the cc prebuilt module enabled for the arm64 target. But the snapshot wasn\u0027t created for the target - i.e. the *.so file doesn\u0027t exist.\n\nWith this change, followed by the update of the prebuilts which I haven\u0027t uploaded yet, the build error disappears.",
      "parentUuid": "4097a5cb_a9b09132",
      "revId": "016c20fedc7bbac40d6aee809961c20bf29c6d6d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
